      "writtenOn": "2025-05-28T15:20:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As a note for anyone stumbling across this review who is wondering why this simplification was made (or not made in the first place):\n\nOriginally, we intended to expose subpass makeup more at the graphite level. After conversations with Shahbaz, it was determined that this is actually likely unideal and introduces complications with minimal benefit. Additionally, we suspect we are actually able to load MSAA from resolve with dynamic rendering after all (in 2 different render passes which theoretically should not be a huge performance hit). Devices adhering to Vulkan profile requirements going forward will have support for dynamic rendering (available in Vulkan 1.3 onward). \n\nThe minimum version for graphite is still 1.1 to accommodate devices released before this requirement (which may later update drivers), so while we want to preserve functionality with that more outdated driver, we now care less about having the pipeline keys be as meticulous and granular seeing as subpass makeup will be less flexible.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "fedce8c9267a0534d3aec14b40c14f3b5599f520",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d5c6f80e_d2d81a36",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 20444
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-28T22:00:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For future reference, the load-msaa-from-resolve (unresolve, as I call it) cannot in fact be done efficiently with dynamic rendering, but:\n\n* VK_EXT_multisampled_render_to_single_sampled solves this for tilers\n* Where not available (desktop GPUs), two-subpass render pass and two render passes are identical in performance (i.e. dynamic rendering works, just with two render passes)",
      "parentUuid": "e19db2bc_bf898815",
      "range": {
